WasmFS: every backend failure to look up a file is reported as ENOENT

Directory::getChild() could only return null, so path lookup, open(),
mkdir(), unlink(), rename() and symlink() took every backend failure for
a missing file: ENOENT, or, for mkdir() and symlink(), an attempt to
create one. It now returns a MaybeFile, which carries a negative error
code; the callers pass it on. The Node backend reports the host's
(EACCES, ENOTDIR, ...; EIO for a host code with no errno), and the OPFS
backend its EIO, or ENOTDIR when the entry changes kind between its two
lookups. Backends that still return plain null get ENOENT, as before.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-lookup-errors.md

